title: The KPD launches a revolution!
new-page: true
subtitle: They claim it is time for the German Soviet...
view-if: revolution_progress >= 10, month == 10
max-visits: 1
go-to: betrayal if in_popular_front or in_left_front; gov_response if spd_in_government; oppo_response if not spd_in_government
tags: event

= The October Revolt

Outraged by recent policy decisions, the KPD has mobilized the RFB and its supporters. A general strike has been declared and the RFB has been called to fight.

The situation is heating up, fast. Barricades are constructed, armed civilians patrol the streets, and isolated firefights have broken out across Berlin. We must do something about the situation.

@betrayal
on-arrival: new_middle_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; rural_spd -= 3; z_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 10; dvp_relation -= 10; lvp_relation -= 10

The KPD has used its position in government to sabotage and infiltrate government institutions, weakening our potential responses. We, of course, receive the brunt of the blame-perhaps rightfully so.

- @join
- @ask_nicely
- @suppress
- @crush

@gov_response

Our position in government gives us advantages in dealing with this revolt, but could also prove a liability.

- @join
- @ask_nicely
- @suppress
- @crush

@oppo_response

- @join
- @quiet
- @condemn

@join
title: Capitalism is buckling at the knees; the time for action is NOW!
choose-if: left_strength >= reformist_strength + center_strength // 2 and kpd_relation >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength < reformist strength + center strength // 2: The bulk of our party prioritizes the Republic over socialism. ?][? if kpd_relation < 60: The KPD refuses to cooperate with us. ?]
on-arrival: kpd_relation += 15; z_relation -= 20; ddp_relation -= 20; dvp_relation -= 20
placeholder for a goto revolutionary civil war event which does not yet exist

@ask_nicely
title: Perhaps we can convince the KPD and workers to stand down?
choose-if: left_strength >= reformist_strength and kpd_relation >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength < reformist_strength: Our reformist elements have written off the KPD as revolutionary zealots. ?][? if kpd_relation < 40: The KPD refuses to even hear us out. ?]
go-to: ask_nicely_yay if kpd_relation // 5 > rfb_force; ask_nicely_nay if kpd_relation // 5 < rfb_force
placeholder here; this has to be reworked to factor in the KPD's chances of success, then the relations. If the KPD are losing at 35/65 or less, there is no way the SPD is convincing them. As that number goes down, high KPD relation can make them stop.

@suppress
title: We must contain the revolt without escalating the situation.
subtitle: We will deploy the Reichsbanner and police to maintain order in the streets.
go-to: suppress_yay if kpd_relation > 50; suppress_nay if kpd_relation < 50; suppress_mid if kpd_relation == 50
placeholder here; this factors in police, reichswehr, and interior power + loyalty, plus reichsbanner power, plus spd worker support, versus kpd worker support and rfb power.

@crush
title: Deploy the Reichswehr to crush this revolt!
go-to: crush_yay if kpd_relation > 50; crush_nay if kpd_relation <= 50
placeholder here; this is based on ONLY paramilitary stuff. there is no middle option--either you destroy it or there's a civil war.
                       
